 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Scene NeRF](12484-scene-nerf.md)
-Isolates static background by training exclusively on background pixels, using an emptiness regularizer.
+Isolates and renders the static background of a scene by training exclusively on background pixels identified via segmentation masks, using an emptiness regularizer to prevent artifacts. Choose it when dynamic foreground elements must be excluded from the neural representation.
 
 ### [NeRF-OSR](14477-nerf-osr.md)
-Outdoor scene relighting that decomposes scene into geometry, albedo, and illumination for physical relighting.
+Learns a neural representation of outdoor scene geometry, diffuse albedo, and illumination-dependent shadows for simultaneous lighting and viewpoint editing. It sets itself apart by providing explicit intrinsic decomposition rather than just view-dependent appearance, enabling physical relighting.
 
 ### [Explicit Volumetric Rendering with Multiple View Aggregation](15335-explicit-volumetric-rendering-with-multiple-view-aggregation.md)
-Models scene as an explicit RGB$\alpha$ volume to amortize rendering across views, enabling real-time rendering and SSIM losses.
+Models scene geometry and appearance as an explicit RGB$\alpha$ volume to amortize rendering across multiple views. Choose it when real-time rendering and structural losses like SSIM are required, avoiding independent per-ray sampling.
 
 ### [Dynamic Neural Radiance Fields](16398-dynamic-neural-radiance-fields.md)
-Models dynamic human faces using a morphable model conditioned on expression parameters and latent codes, requiring only monocular input.
+Models the appearance and dynamics of a human face using an implicit volumetric representation conditioned on morphable model expression parameters and per-frame latent codes. Choose it when handling dynamically changing surfaces from monocular input is necessary.
 
 ### [Neural Network Pruning for NeRF](17703-neural-network-pruning-for-nerf.md)
-Compresses NeRF by pruning small-magnitude MLP weights, reducing storage and inference time.
+Compresses a NeRF by removing weights with the smallest magnitudes from the fully-connected network. Choose it when reducing storage size and inference time is prioritized over structural scene changes.
 
 ### [Scene Auto-Encoder](17789-scene-auto-encoder.md)
-Encodes RGB images into discrete density and feature voxel grids via 2D CNN encoder and frustum lifting.
+Encodes RGB images with known poses and depth into 3D neural fields represented as density and feature voxel grids via a 2D CNN encoder and frustum lifting. Choose it when discrete voxel-based representations and latent compression are needed.
 
 ### [Bi-level Neural Volume Fusion](19888-bi-level-neural-volume-fusion.md)
-Incrementally integrates noisy depth maps into a global neural implicit representation using local weighted averaging and global neural rendering optimization.
+Incrementally integrates noisy depth maps into a global neural implicit representation using local weighted averaging and global neural rendering optimization. Choose it when geometric coherence and scalability are required for dense 3D reconstruction.
 
 ### [Neural Radiance Field Codebooks (NRC)](21345-neural-radiance-field-codebooks-nrc.md)
-Maps continuous spatial features to a discrete codebook for scalable, object-centric representations with constant rendering compute.
+Maps continuous spatial features to a discrete, finite codebook of object categories for scalable, object-centric representations. Choose it when constant rendering compute regardless of object count and unbounded object support are needed.
 
 ### Mask Inverse Rendering
-Projects 2D masks from SAM into 3D space to form 3D masks. Optimizes volume values $V(r(t))$ or mask values $m_{gi}$ to increase confidence where SAM predicts foreground. Uses loss $L_{proj} = - \sum_{r \in R(I)} MSAM(r) \cdot M(r)$, potentially with a negative refinement term $\lambda \sum (1 - MSAM(r)) \cdot M(r)$ to handle SAM inaccuracies [S5].
+Projects 2D masks from SAM into 3D space to form 3D masks based on ray weights. It optimizes volume values $V(r(t))$ or mask values $m_{gi}$ to increase confidence where SAM predicts foreground, using a negative refinement term to handle SAM inaccuracies across views. Choose it for 3D segmentation and object isolation using radiance fields [S5].
 
